do you formulate to counteract some of the

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.850
CNN and MSNBC talking points like that?

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.690
Well, it fits in a family situation.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:55.600
I've said before, I would simply just try
to inquire as to how they came to those conclusions.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.160
So when they say Bernie's gone too far left,
I would say, what's an example?

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.160
Policy?

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.840
And then either they won't have anything or
they'll say, well, his health care plan is

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:04.840
too far left.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.720
And then you say, well why do you think that
so many countries have been able to do what

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.930
Bernie is proposing?

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.170
And it's working better than what we have
here.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:17.600
Or, uh, if they say Elizabeth Warren's wealth
tax would, uh, would never work, or it would

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.270
never pass or whatever, then you say, Oh,
do you not think that inequality is a problem?

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.270
Oh, you do.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.560
Well, how would you solve it?

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.909
I think that using the respectful, probing
questions, especially in family situations,

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:31.440
is the way to go.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.970
You know, at rather than saying you've been
brainwashed by corporate media, that that's

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.180
less likely to get people to really examine
their beliefs.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.180
Yeah.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.540
That I knew not to take that approach.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.540
I did.

